<title>FRANCE: U.S. main destination for Q1 ex-Paris airfreight.</title>
<headline>U.S. main destination for Q1 ex-Paris airfreight.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in January-March 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations by country for ADP exports in January-March 1997, with percentage change on January-March 1996 in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>1.  United States     30,153 tonnes   (+7.1 percent)</p>
<p>2.  Japan		  7,692 tonnes  (-14.0)</p>
<p>3.  Germany		5,817 tonnes  (+27.3)</p>
<p>4.  Hong Kong	    5,340 tonnes   (+2.3)</p>
<p>5.  UK		     4,945 tonnes  (+43.7)</p>
<p>6.  Canada		 4,832 tonnes  (-10.2)</p>
<p>7.  Brazil		 4,252 tonnes  (+31.8)</p>
<p>8.  U.A.E.		 3,853 tonnes  (+18.3)</p>
<p>9.  Mexico		 3,226 tonnes  (+11.6)</p>
<p>10. India		  3,086 tonnes  (-17.1)</p>
<p>11. Fr.W Indies	  2,876 tonnes  (-10.0)</p>
<p>12. Singapore	    2,854 tonnes  (+52.9)</p>
<p>13. Saudi Arabia	 2,531 tonnes  (-12.9)</p>
<p>14. Reunion		2,327 tonnes   (-5.2)</p>
<p>15. Thailand	     2,198 tonnes  (+20.5)</p>
<p>16. Egypt		  1,982 tonnes   (-7.7)</p>
<p>17. Korea		  1,917 tonnes   (-2.5)</p>
<p>18. Italy		  1,884 tonnes  (-18.9)</p>
<p>19. Lebanon		1,830 tonnes   (+6.7)</p>
<p>20. China		  1,489 tonnes  (-18.8)</p>
<p>A total 138,816 tonnes of air cargo exports left the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in January- March 1997, up 1.2 percent on the same period last year , airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel +44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
